# Starlit configuration — copy to secrets.env (or export these) and fill in what you need.
# Starlit runs with NO configuration: every value below has a working default for a git clone.
# A DeepSeek key is optional — without it, unrecognised rows are simply reported UNVERIFIED.

# Where the app keeps app.db, charts/ and uploads/.  Default: ./data beside the code.
# STARLIT_DATA=/var/lib/starlit

# The engine package, if it lives somewhere unusual.  Default: ./engine beside the code.
# STARLIT_ENGINE=

# The file holding the DeepSeek API key (a line like DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...).
# Default: ./secrets.env beside the code.
# STARLIT_SECRETS=

# Bind address / port for the built-in server.  Defaults: 127.0.0.1:6090.
# STARLIT_HOST=127.0.0.1
# STARLIT_PORT=6090

# Only needed for the optional LLM fallback (a vocabulary widener for clauses the rules do not
# recognise).  Without it, those rows are reported UNVERIFIED and everything else still works.
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...
